  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a gate-based quantum graph neural network for credit card fraud detection using angle encoding and a variational circuit with Rx, Ry, and CNOT gates. On the public ULB/Kaggle dataset of 284,807 transactions with 492 frauds, the best QGNN configuration (6 qubits, 1 layer) achieved 94.5% accuracy, 96.1% precision, 79.5% recall, 0.86 F1, and about 0.85 PR-AUC, compared with GraphSAGE at 92.3% accuracy, 95.2% precision, 76.3% recall, 0.83 F1, and 0.77 ROC-AUC.",
